// SET S2 (stretch builder, 2026-11-15, ROUGH BOARD): THE HERO'S CHURCH, two modes picked by film.json places.<name>.mode.
//  mode "inside" (PICTURE PLAN rows 8-11, light B candle): the nave south of the hero tower. Gold altar on red steps at the east end, deep red dossal cloth,
//    blue barrel vault with gold stars and gold ribs, rows of iron candle stands, walnut benches, red carpet runner, tiled floor. In the north wall the SIDE DOOR
//    (two leaves open inward) looks onto the tower's south wall 1.4 m outside, where THE IRON WIRE runs down with staples into a mud patch; above the door the
//    HIGH WINDOW shows the tower top with THE SPEAR against the violet dusk.
//    STAGE CHEAT (told to the lead in STATE.md): in this mode the tower TOP is built with its peak 8.5 m above the church floor (true: 31 m), because from
//    inside a nave the real tip stands 70-80 degrees up and is hidden by its own roof edge. The lower shaft, the wire and its place (x .5, y -1.62) are true.
//  mode "steps" (rows 19-20, light E spring drizzle that stops, then one sunbeam): the paved parvis and steps in front of the church, local frame turned so
//    +Y' points at RIVAL. Far: the white marble tower (banded shaft, open belfry with the swinging bronze bell and the tiny ringer on the rope, WOODEN roof,
//    gold angel), cypress road, far hill, the vineyard ridge with the one old tree, town roofs left and right of the white road. Near: steps, wet paving,
//    balustrade, pink blossom branch, the church front with its door. The hero tower stands at its true place and height (origin) for the look up to the spear.
